# Otter Web API Server Example (D51)
# Readable HTTP services with routes and JSON responses

api is a web server
    port is 8080
    host is "localhost"
.

when api receives GET at "/health"
    respond with "OK"
.

when api receives GET at "/api/greeting"
    respond with "Hello from Otter Web Server!"
.

when api receives GET at "/api/users"
    respond with "Ada Lovelace" as json
.

when api receives POST at "/api/users" into req
    respond with "User created" as json and status 201
.

start api
